# SMOKE RUN in a container: EVERY FIGURE IN THIS LOG IS INSTRUMENTATION, NOT A RESULT (README 1.1)
# engine:         BenchmarkDotNet 0.15.8.0 (CAMPAIGN.md 22a), toolchain InProcessEmit (this process, pinned by the runner)
# runtime:        .NET 8.0.31; TieredCompilation=default TieredPGO=default (net8.0 defaults unless set); GC server=False, concurrent (default)
# incumbent:      Google.Protobuf 3.32.0
# build:          full (WP5 step 10; the loaded core checked to be the same variant by its u-family exports)
# managed codec:  plan utf8=reject unknown=drop
# job:            launch 1; 1 actual iterations (rounds) per case, 1 warm-up iterations (the same for every case) after BDN's jitting stage (1 overhead + 1 workload jitting invocation per case, logged by BDN in the .bdn.log, not exported) and pilot, iteration time 2 ms (the pilot picks the invocation count per case), strategy Throughput, EvaluateOverhead=false (no overhead subtraction anywhere)
# clocks:         per iteration (every row with round >= 1): wall (Stopwatch) AND process CPU (CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID of this process: every thread, GC and JIT included; CAMPAIGN req 21 as amended, R-H25), both read by the job's clock (CpuClock, Job.WithClock) at the start and end of the same iteration window, exported RAW (no outlier removal, no overhead subtraction); BDN's forced GCs between iterations are outside the window; the round-0 row of each case is a summary of the whole actual stage (span_cpu_ns, span_wall_ns), not a sample
# threads:        thread pool min 1 worker / 1 IO, max 32767 worker / 1000 IO, 0 pool thread(s) now; 1 logical CPUs visible; the codec suite creates no core runtime (no RPC call is made); the timed loop runs on BDN's one thread
# encode:         CAMPAIGN req 11 (R-H29): dir encode = pool input + reused buffer; encode-hot = one graph + reused buffer; encode-transport = pool + the Grpc.Net form; encode-transport-hot = one graph + the Grpc.Net form. Reused buffer: incumbent-prod CalculateSize + WriteTo(IBufferWriter) and incumbent-best WriteTo(IBufferWriter) into one BufWriter, host-gen into its one Enc, core-ffi into the core's encode buffer (ak_encode_*/ak_uencode_*; that buffer is also what cell C hands the core's transport, and host-gen's Enc what cell E hands it, so their transport forms on the core's transport ARE the buffer rows). Grpc.Net form (cells A, F, D): the serializer the RPC grid's marshaller runs (RootOps.SerInc/SerHost/SerFfi), into a frame like Grpc.Net.Client 2.71's GrpcCallSerializationContext: one ArrayPool array, the 5-byte gRPC header, the body, the array returned after (GrpcFrame.cs); incumbent-best has no gRPC path and no transport row. Pool: distinct graphs built in the case's setup whose RETAINED heap is >= 65536 bytes (2 x AK_LLC_BYTES, default 13.75 MB; AK_POOL_BYTES overrides; per row pool_graphs and pool_bytes), round robin one graph per call; a hot input is a pool of one (the same Next() per call); graph construction is never in the timed window
# U-* rows:       CAMPAIGN req 7 (R-H27): the 92 accepted, non-disputed U-* rows at the shapes core's 7 ABI roots, through this timed shapes core: encode-hot (a graph the arm decoded from the row, untimed; retain arms re-emit the unknown fields, drop arms the dropped form), decode, decode-read, and decode-reencode (a labelled extra; no incumbent-best row)
# content sets:   CAMPAIGN req 7 (R-H26): ascii, latin1 and wide on P1.2, P2.2, P2.4; ascii only elsewhere
# order:          seeded shuffles (below); ratios, where the aggregation forms them, come from per-launch medians (CAMPAIGN req 30): every unit is its own process
# process unit:   core-ffi-pull:drop; this launch's unit order: core-ffi:retain, incumbent-prod:default, core-ffi:drop, host-gen:retain, core-ffi-pull:drop, host-gen:drop, incumbent-best:default (a seeded shuffle, seed 7919; within this process the cases run in a seeded shuffle too, seed 104729, the 2 prime cases first; requirement 22 as amended, R-H23)
# pre-warm:       9 round(s) of 64 calls to every case of this process, 0.5 s apart, before BDN starts; the last round compiled 0 method(s) of measured code (JIT events read back)
# correctness:    1496 pre-timing checks passed (byte identity of every encode arm per payload and content set; every arm accepts every unknown row; on every unknown row core-ffi retain and host-gen retain re-encode to the incumbent's bytes, i.e. the unknown fields are kept: requirement 10)
# cases:          44 exported, after 2 prime case(s) run first and not exported (copies of the first cases, content "prime")
